# semgrep ships a default .semgrepignore that excludes `tests/` and `test/`. Because a
# repository's own file replaces that default rather than adding to it, this file is how
# sprout's test suite gets scanned at all: naming `tests` on the command line scanned
# ZERO files while the default was in force, so the SAST gate reported success over the
# 48 tracked Python files under tests/ without reading one of them.
#
# semgrep only ever scans git-tracked files, so the default's other entries (.venv/,
# node_modules/, dist/, build/) are already excluded by not being tracked, and nothing
# here needs to repeat them. tests/test_security_gate.py fails if a directory holding
# tracked Python is excluded here or missing from the Makefile's SAST_PATHS.

# The TS port has its own toolchain (npm run typecheck / npm test) and is not Python.
web-static/node_modules/
web-static/public/
web-static/test/fixtures/

# Generated artifacts, not source.
site/
var/
